1. `fetchGithubCheckLogs` resolves logs from details_url via two shapes only: `/jobs/{id}` and `/actions/runs/{id}` (workflow run). A bare check-run URL `https://github.com/o/runs/{id}` (GitHub's canonical check-run page URL) matches neither the job pattern nor the actions-run pattern meaningfully — actually it DOES match `/\/runs\/(\d+)/` in `extractGithubRunId`, so the **check-run id** is misinterpreted as a **workflow-run id** and passed to `github_get_workflow_run_jobs`, which cannot resolve it → null → silent per-check skip.
2. Failures are silent: when no logs resolve for a check, nothing is recorded in `ci_failures.md` or `ci_failures_full.log`.
3. `buildCiFailuresHeader` unconditionally advertises `ci_failures_full.log`, and `buildCiFailuresResolutionSection` unconditionally points at it — even when no full log will be written.
4. The full log is only written when at least one check produced logs; nothing marks the checks that failed to resolve.

## Fix plan (githubHelpers.js)

New/changed pieces:

1. `extractGithubCheckRunId(check)` — extracts a **bare** check-run id: `/\/runs\/(\d+)/` NOT preceded by `/actions/`. Implementation: 
  ```js
  function extractGithubCheckRunId(check) {
      var url = check && check.details_url ? String(check.details_url) : '';
      if (!url) return null;
      if (/\/actions\/runs\/\d+/.test(url)) return null; // workflow-run URL, handled by the run path
      var m = url.match(/\/runs\/(\d+)/);
      return m ? m[1] : null;
  }
  ```

2. `fetchGithubCheckRunLogs(check, scm, owner, repo)` — gh-1045: bare check-run URL → the id IS a check-run id; GitHub's jobs/log endpoints accept a check-run id directly → `_fetchJobLogs(scm, owner, repo, checkRunId)`. Wrap in try/catch → null on failure.

3. `fetchGithubCheckLogs` fallback chain becomes:
  ```js
  function fetchGithubCheckLogs(check, scm, owner, repo) {
      var jobIdMatch = ...; if (jobIdMatch) { existing }
      // /actions/runs/N[/job/M] — workflow-run path (gh-982)
      if (/\/actions\/runs\/\d+/.test(url)) return fetchGithubRunLogs(check, scm, owner, repo);
      // gh-1045: bare check-run URL (github.com/o/runs/N) — check-run id
      var checkRunId = extractGithubCheckRunId(check);
      if (checkRunId) return fetchGithubCheckRunLogs(check, scm, owner, repo, checkRunId);
      return null;
  }
  ```
