1. `fetchGithubCheckLogs` resolves logs from details_url via two shapes only: `/jobs/{id}` and `/actions/runs/{id}` (workflow run). A bare check-run URL `https://github.com/o/runs/{id}` (GitHub's canonical check-run page URL) matches neither the job pattern nor the actions-run pattern meaningfully — actually it DOES match `/\/runs\/(\d+)/` in `extractGithubRunId`, so the **check-run id** is misinterpreted as a **workflow-run id** and passed to `github_get_workflow_run_jobs`, which cannot resolve it → null → silent per-check skip.
